  "title": "3 · Schedules & Serializability (Unit 3)",
  "learn": "<h3>Schedule</h3><p>A <b>schedule</b> is the chronological ordering of the operations of several transactions. A <b>serial</b> schedule never interleaves transactions, so it is always consistent, but it limits concurrency and wastes CPU. A <b>complete</b> schedule ends every transaction with commit or abort.</p>\n<h3>Recoverability</h3><p><b>Recoverable</b>: if Tj reads data written by Ti, Ti must commit before Tj. <b>Non-recoverable</b>: Tj reads Ti's dirty value and commits first; if Ti then fails, Tj cannot be rolled back. <b>Cascading rollback</b>: one failure forces dependent transactions to abort. <b>Cascadeless</b>: a transaction reads a value only after the writer commits. <b>Strict</b>: no read or overwrite until the writer commits or aborts. Every strict schedule is recoverable and cascadeless.</p>\n<h3>Conflict serializability</h3><p>Conflicting pairs on the same item by different transactions: <b>R-W, W-R, W-W</b>. Draw a <b>precedence graph</b> (edge Ti → Tj if Ti's conflicting operation comes first). A schedule is <b>conflict serializable if and only if the graph has no cycle</b>.</p>\n<p><i>Example:</i> S: R1(x) R2(x) W1(x) R1(y) W2(x) W1(y). R2(x) before W1(x) gives 2→1; R1(x) before W2(x) gives 1→2. Cycle, so <b>not</b> conflict serializable.</p>\n<h3>View serializability</h3><p>A schedule is <b>view serializable</b> if it is view equivalent to a serial schedule: same <b>initial reads</b>, same <b>update (write-read) sources</b> and same <b>final writes</b>. Every conflict-serializable schedule is view serializable, but not the other way round.</p><figure style=\"margin:14px 0\"><svg class=\"dg\" viewBox=\"0 0 640 190\"><defs><marker id=\"ar\" markerWidth=\"9\" markerHeight=\"9\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"4.5\" orient=\"auto\"><path class=\"dg-arr\" d=\"M0,0L9,4.5L0,9z\"/></marker><marker id=\"ar2\" markerWidth=\"9\" markerHeight=\"9\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"4.5\" orient=\"auto\"><path class=\"dg-arr2\" d=\"M0,0L9,4.5L0,9z\"/></marker></defs><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"10\" y=\"10\" width=\"420\" height=\"170\" rx=\"12\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"220\" y=\"28\" text-anchor=\"middle\">All schedules</text><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"44\" y=\"36\" width=\"352\" height=\"118\" rx=\"12\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"220\" y=\"54\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Recoverable</text><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"78\" y=\"62\" width=\"284\" height=\"66\" rx=\"12\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"220\" y=\"80\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Cascadeless</text><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"112\" y=\"88\" width=\"216\" height=\"14\" rx=\"12\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"220\" y=\"106\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Strict</text><text class=\"dg-m\" x=\"450\" y=\"60\" text-anchor=\"start\">Outside = non-recoverable</text></svg><figcaption class=\"mu\" style=\"text-align:center\">Figure 5: strict ⊂ cascadeless ⊂ recoverable ⊂ all schedules</figcaption></figure><figure style=\"margin:14px 0\"><svg class=\"dg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 180\"><defs><marker id=\"ar\" markerWidth=\"9\" markerHeight=\"9\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"4.5\" orient=\"auto\"><path class=\"dg-arr\" d=\"M0,0L9,4.5L0,9z\"/></marker><marker id=\"ar2\" markerWidth=\"9\" markerHeight=\"9\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"4.5\" orient=\"auto\"><path class=\"dg-arr2\" d=\"M0,0L9,4.5L0,9z\"/></marker></defs><rect class=\"dg-hd\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"150\" height=\"26\"/><text class=\"dg-th\" x=\"75.0\" y=\"18.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T1</text><rect class=\"dg-hd\" x=\"150\" y=\"0\" width=\"150\" height=\"26\"/><text class=\"dg-th\" x=\"225.0\" y=\"18.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T2</text><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"2\" y=\"28\" width=\"146\" height=\"22\" rx=\"5\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"75.0\" y=\"44.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">R(x); x = x + 10; W(x)</text><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"152\" y=\"54\" width=\"146\" height=\"22\" rx=\"5\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"225.0\" y=\"70.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">R(x); x = x − 5; W(x)</text><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"152\" y=\"80\" width=\"146\" height=\"22\" rx=\"5\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"225.0\" y=\"96.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Commit</text><rect class=\"dg-bad\" x=\"2\" y=\"106\" width=\"146\" height=\"22\" rx=\"5\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"75.0\" y=\"122.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">FAIL</text><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"2\" y=\"132\" width=\"146\" height=\"22\" rx=\"5\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"75.0\" y=\"148.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Commit</text><text class=\"dg-m\" x=\"150.0\" y=\"174\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T2 read T1's dirty value and committed first, so it cannot be undone</text></svg><figcaption class=\"mu\" style=\"text-align:center\">Figure 6: a non-recoverable schedule</figcaption></figure><figure style=\"margin:14px 0\"><svg class=\"dg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 180\"><defs><marker id=\"ar\" markerWidth=\"9\" markerHeight=\"9\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"4.5\" orient=\"auto\"><path class=\"dg-arr\" d=\"M0,0L9,4.5L0,9z\"/></marker><marker id=\"ar2\" markerWidth=\"9\" markerHeight=\"9\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"4.5\" orient=\"auto\"><path class=\"dg-arr2\" d=\"M0,0L9,4.5L0,9z\"/></marker></defs><line class=\"dg-r\" x1=\"104.0\" y1=\"104.0\" x2=\"194.0\" y2=\"104.0\" marker-end=\"url(#ar2)\"/><line class=\"dg-r\" x1=\"196.0\" y1=\"76.0\" x2=\"106.0\" y2=\"76.0\" marker-end=\"url(#ar2)\"/><circle class=\"dg-box\" cx=\"80\" cy=\"90\" r=\"22\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"80\" y=\"95\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T1</text><circle class=\"dg-box\" cx=\"220\" cy=\"90\" r=\"22\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"220\" y=\"95\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T2</text></svg><figcaption class=\"mu\" style=\"text-align:center\">Figure 7: precedence graph of R1(x) R2(x) W1(x) R1(y) W2(x) W1(y): a cycle, so NOT conflict serializable</figcaption></figure><figure style=\"margin:14px 0\"><svg class=\"dg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 180\"><defs><marker id=\"ar\" markerWidth=\"9\" markerHeight=\"9\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"4.5\" orient=\"auto\"><path class=\"dg-arr\" d=\"M0,0L9,4.5L0,9z\"/></marker><marker id=\"ar2\" markerWidth=\"9\" markerHeight=\"9\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"4.5\" orient=\"auto\"><path class=\"dg-arr2\" d=\"M0,0L9,4.5L0,9z\"/></marker></defs><line class=\"dg-ln\" x1=\"104.0\" y1=\"90.0\" x2=\"194.0\" y2=\"90.0\" marker-end=\"url(#ar)\"/><circle class=\"dg-box\" cx=\"80\" cy=\"90\" r=\"22\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"80\" y=\"95\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T1</text><circle class=\"dg-box\" cx=\"220\" cy=\"90\" r=\"22\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"220\" y=\"95\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T2</text></svg><figcaption class=\"mu\" style=\"text-align:center\">Figure 8: R1(A) W1(A) R2(A) W2(A) R1(B) W1(B): one edge, acyclic, so conflict serializable (T1 then T2)</figcaption></figure><h3>View-equivalence checklist</h3><p>Compare S1 with a serial schedule S2: (1) <b>initial reads</b> by the same transactions, (2) the same <b>update sources</b> (who reads whose write), (3) the same <b>final writes</b>. If all match, S1 is view serializable. Steps to test conflict serializability: list conflicting pairs, draw an edge for each, look for a cycle.</p>",
